      "description": "Watch Plymouth vs Coventry highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. The atmosphere was electric as two determined sides met in a cup clash that promised goals and high-intensity football from the very first whistle. Momentum swung back and forth throughout the evening, keeping the crowd on the edge of their seats as the tactical battle unfolded. Rapid Start for the Visitors On August 25, 2026, Coventry City wasted no time establishing dominance in this Carabao Cup fixture. Just three minutes in, Taiwo Awoniyi found the bottom right corner following a clinical through ball from Caleb Yirenkyi . Before the home crowd could catch their breath, Jack Rudoni doubled the lead in the 5th minute, finishing a move started by Awoniyi to put Plymouth Argyle on the ropes early in the contest. Argyle Claw Back Despite the nightmare start, Plymouth Argyle found a lifeline in the 21st minute when Oliver Irow finished a clinical fast break initiated by Harvey White . The home side grew in confidence and sustained their pressure into the second half. In the 54th minute, substitute Xavier Amaechi struck a low left-footed shot into the corner to bring the scores level at 2-2, igniting hope of a complete turnaround among the home faithful. Coventry Reclaim Control The parity lasted until the 67th minute when Ephron Mason-Clark , having just come off the bench, restored Coventry City 's lead from very close range. The pressure mounted on the hosts, and in the 77th minute, Joe Edwards conceded a penalty. Victor Torp stepped up and coolly dispatched the spot-kick into the top right corner, effectively ending the contest. Despite late efforts from Brandon Thomas-Asante , the visitors held firm to secure their 4-2 victory and progression."
